        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikhail Glinka, Jean-Baptiste Lully, Alexey Verstovsky\n- Roles: composer, instrumentalist, dancer, musical bureaucrat\n- Places: Russia, France\n- Concepts: Russian classical music, court of Louis XIV\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully, born Giovanni Battista Lulli, lived from 28 November 1632 to 22 March 1687.\n- Jean-Baptiste Lully was an Italian-born French composer, instrumentalist, and dancer who spent most of his life working in the court of Louis XIV of France.\n- Alexey Verstovsky lived from 1 March 1799 to 17 November 1862.\n- Mikhail Glinka lived from 1 June 1804 to 15 February 1857.\n- Alexey Verstovsky was a Russian composer and musical bureaucrat who was a rival of Mikhail Glinka.\n- Mikhail Glinka was the first Russian composer to gain wide recognition within Russia and is often regarded as the fountainhead of Russian classical music.",
